#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:100
msgid "What are the game columns?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:101
msgid ""
"\n"
"    Available Games - Games that are available to join and are not waiting "
"for a repsonse from invited players<BR />\n"
"    Current Games - Games you are currently playing<BR />\n"
"    Waiting Games - Games you have joined, but are waiting for more players "
"(either invited players or open to anyone)<BR />\n"
"    Invitations - Games you have been invited to play<BR />\n"
"    Finished Games - Your finished games. Games you have resigned or been "
"kicked from will stop showing under \"Current Games\" but will show here "
"once they are finished<BR />\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    If you create a game open to anyone, it will be shown under your "
"\"Waiting Games\" and also visible in \"Available Games\".<BR />\n"
"    If you create a game and invite other players, it will be shown under "
"your \"Waiting Games\" only, until all invited players have responded.<BR /"
">\n"
"    <B><U>How can I laave a game that hasn't started?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    Under \"Waiting Games\" there is a \"Leave\" button on the right. If you "
"are not waiting for specific players to join, you can also see the game "
"under \"Available Games\", with a \"Leave\" button on the left.<BR />\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:117
msgid "Profile Setup"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:120
msgid ""
"\n"
"    <B><U>What are the notifications?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    All games update live, so you can set whether you wish to hear a beep, "
"bell, or nothing if a game comes to your turn\n"
"    whilst the game page is open.<BR />\n"
"    In addition, you can add email notifications, discord notifications, and "
"slack notifications<BR />\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>How can I add a Discord Notification?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    You can add Discord notifications to one of your servers, or an existing "
"server where you have administrator\n"
"    privileges.<BR />\n"
"    To set up your own free server, <a\n"
"      href=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/articles/204849977-How-do-"
"I-create-a-server-\" target=\"_blank\">click\n"
"      here</a>.<BR />\n"
"    To set up a webhook and find the URL to copy into your Online Board "
"Gamers Profile, <a\n"
"      href=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/articles/228383668-Intro-"
"to-Webhooks\" target=\"_blank\">click\n"
"      here</a>.<BR />\n"
"    Follow the guide to set up a webhook and \"Copy Webhook URL\". Then "
"paste the link in to your profile on Online Board\n"
"    Gamers. <BR />\n"
"    Note that Discord notifications will be sent to a channel, not to your "
"private messages. <BR />\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>How can I add a Slack Notification?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    Create a slack app and enable/create an incoming Webhook. Set it to post "
"to a channel or your private messages. Then\n"
"    paste the link in to your profile on Online Board Gamers.<BR />\n"
"    For details on each step, <a href=\"https://api.slack.com/messaging/"
"webhooks\" target=\"_blank\">click here</a>.<BR />\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:150
msgid "Game Setup"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:153
msgid ""
"\n"
"    <B><U>What does the Playing Speed option do?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    The Playing Speed option mainly gives other players an idea of how fast "
"you want the game to play. It is also\n"
"    linked to the options for the length of time before an inactive player "
"is removed.\n"
"    Blitz Dual is limited to 2 player, and has optiona from 5 minutes to 20 "
"minutes. Live speed allows kickouts of 12\n"
"    hours or 1 day. The other speeds allow kickouts between 1 day and 5 "
"days.\n"
"    Please note that often with 4 or more random players then more than 1 or "
"2 moves a day could be difficult,\n"
"    especially if\n"
"    people are in different time zones. With 2 or 3 players however,\n"
"    it is certainly possible to play several games in an evening!<BR />\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>How much time do I have left in a Blitz Dual speed game?</U></"
"B><BR />\n"
"    You can see a timer counting down to the next kickout in the top right, "
"underneath where it says who you are logged\n"
"    in as.\n"
"    In fact, any game that is within 20 minutes of a kickout will display "
"the timer. There is a short grace period once\n"
"    the timer reaches zero,\n"
"    and no one is kicked until a player enters the game who isn't currently "
"required to move, thus activiating the\n"
"    kickout.\n"
"    All games will auto-update live, but if you are playing Blitz Dual and "
"your opponent doesn't appear to be moving,\n"
"    then it is worth refreshing the game,\n"
"    in case you lost internet signal at the same time the game update signal "
"arrived.<BR />\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>Where do the FCM scenarios come from?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    They are suggested in the Ketchup Expansion manual. <BR />\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\Lobby\lobbyHelp.html:184
msgid ""
"\n"
"    <B><U>What are the formats?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    Knockout is simply the winner moves to the next round. Two Lives is like "
"double elimination; once you've lose twice then you're out of the "
"tournament. Rounds consists of\n"
"    (currently) 4 rounds, where all players are included in the games, after "
"which there is a short knockout of all players on top points to determine "
"the overall winner. <BR />\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>How are game players decided?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    Initially game players are drawn randomly. After this, players are "
"ranked by number of wins. Players will play the closest person to them that "
"thay haven't already played. <BR/>\n"
"    If there are any players left over, they receive a \"bye\", which counts "
"as an automatic win, and progress to the next round. \"Byes\" will generally "
"be given to the lowest ranked players,\n"
"    and are limited to one per tournament. Essentially \"Byes\" are given "
"randomly to the lowest ranked player who hasn't yet had a \"Bye\".<BR/>\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>How do kickouts work?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    If someone is kicked out then they are ejected from the tournament. They "
"will lose both lives in Two Lives, and be removed from a Rounds tournament "
"<BR/>\n"
"    <BR />\n"
"    <B><U>What else should I know?</U></B><BR />\n"
"    Players will not play the same person again until there's no other "
"option<BR/>\n"
"    Players will not receive two \"byes\" until there's no other option<BR/"
">\n"
"    Kickout timer will be 1 day, with the exception of the first move "
"(restaurant placement) which will be 3 days, in case players don't realise a "
"game has started<BR/>\n"
"    Notifications are sent out at the start of every new tournament game. If "
"you finish quickly there could be several days until your next game starts,\n"
"    so it is strongly recommended to have at least one form of notification "
"enabled in your profile<BR/>\n"
"    I can start a tournament any time, but too many could lead to tournament "
"fatigue! So I'm planning to always have some sort of tournament available or "
"ongoing.\n"
"    Initially, there will be a bit of an open testing phase, as I can't test "
"more than about 5 players myself! After this, there might be one of each "
"tournament that starts\n"
"    at the begining of each month, or one every two weeks, or something<BR/"
">\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

